+`read-saved-history` requires a control link and the history key on every request.
+It takes a listed session id, never a path. It returns the active branch as
+newline-delimited JSON in branch order, without the session header.
+
+Each page carries at most 256 KiB of raw bytes as unpadded base64url in `bytes`.
+Concatenate decoded pages and continue from `nextOffset` until `done` is true.
+A page can split a JSON line, so decode before parsing.
+
+The first reply snapshots the complete-line prefix. Send its `revision` with every
+later request. Later pages use the same snapshot, even while the session grows.
+
+The host can return `unavailable`, `invalid_request`, `not_found`, or `ambiguous`
+for a duplicate session id. It returns `changed` when a prefix changes during a
+copy or the snapshot cannot be rebuilt. Restart a changed read at offset zero,
+without a revision. Replies never include file paths.
+
+The host uses unlinked private files and retains up to eight idle snapshots, with a
+1 GiB total limit. A closed snapshot can be rebuilt while its original prefix remains.
+The prefix copy requires a working `/dev/fd` on the host.
 
 Guests with a view-only link can read everything live — back-transcript, streaming text, tool cards, subagent transcripts — but the host rejects prompting, interrupting, and agent control from them.
 
@@ -229,4 +236,11 @@ Hub topology — the host is authoritative, guests never peer:
 
 Guest→host: `hello`, `prompt`, `abort`, `agent-cmd` (hub chat/kill/revive), `fetch-transcript` (incremental subagent-transcript reads answered by targeted `transcript` frames), `list-saved-sessions` and `read-saved-history` (history-key gated, answered by `saved-sessions` and `saved-history` frames), and `ui-response`. The replica loads through the regular `/resume` machinery, so theming, ctrl+o, and transcript behavior are native by construction; the guest process never chdirs to host paths.
 
+Guests may include an integer `actionId` in prompt, abort, or UI response frames.
+The host sends a targeted `control-result` with the same identifier and an `accepted`
+boolean.
+
+A missing result means the outcome is unknown; do not retry automatically.
+For a prompt, acceptance means admission, not completion of the agent run.
+
 Transcript fetches are capped at 4 MiB per reply and end on complete JSONL lines. Guests continue from `newSize`; a single entry exceeding the cap produces a terminal transcript error instead of an endless empty-read retry.
